## Current step: {{ step }}
{% if step == "requirements" %}
Produce the requirements and constraints list for this automation.

Think about: inputs and outputs, target systems, whether an API (headless) or a browser is needed, data classification
and whether LLM use is allowed on that data, schedule and volume, failure modes, who owns it.

### Worked example
Goal: "Automate the quarterly compliance report on portal Y".
Output:
```json
{"summary": "Quarterly compliance report submission on portal Y",
 "inputs": ["quarter (param)", "figures workbook on the shared path"],
 "outputs": ["submission receipt id", "run summary"],
 "target_systems": [{"name": "portal Y", "access": "browser, user session", "has_api": false}],
 "data_classification": "confidential",
 "llm_allowed": false,
 "schedule": "quarterly, 1st business day 08:00",
 "constraints": ["unattended", "no LLM on confidential figures", "idempotent: do not submit twice"],
 "risks": ["portal layout changes", "session expiry mid-run"],
 "open_questions": []}
```
Return ONLY one JSON object with keys: summary, inputs, outputs, target_systems, data_classification, llm_allowed, schedule, constraints, risks, open_questions.
